# 2. Preserve Existing Ownership

PayKH remains authoritative for:

* Tenants
* Customers
* Merchants
* Orders
* Payment orders
* Campaigns
* Loyalty
* Cashback rules
* Referral rules
* Scratch-game rules
* Merchant settlement instructions

PayChain remains authoritative for:

* Digital assets
* Wallets
* Asset issuance
* Mint transactions
* Burn transactions
* Transfers
* Digital balances
* Redemption asset status

Trustee Platform becomes authoritative for:

* Bank account registry
* Cleared deposits
* Trustee funds
* Safeguarded funds
* Reserve balances
* Mint authorization
* Fiat redemption payout
* Merchant settlement confirmation
* Reserve and safeguarding evidence
* Bank-side reconciliation
* Compliance holds
* Trustee approvals

Do not copy the entire PayChain or PayKH databases into the Trustee Platform.

