# 3. Integration Strategy

Implement adapters:

```text
PayChainAdapter
PayKHAdapter
TrusteeBankAdapter
KHQRProviderAdapter
ComplianceProviderAdapter
```

Each adapter must isolate the Trustee Platform from changes in external systems.

Use:

* REST APIs
* Signed webhooks
* Scheduled reconciliation
* Idempotency keys
* Correlation IDs
* Retry queues
* Dead-letter queues
* Replay controls
* API versioning

---

# 4. PayChain Integration Adapter

Create:

```typescript
interface PayChainAdapter {
  getAsset(assetId: string): Promise<PayChainAsset>;
  getAssetSupply(assetId: string): Promise<AssetSupply>;
  getTransaction(transactionId: string): Promise<PayChainTransaction>;
  getMintStatus(requestId: string): Promise<MintStatus>;
  getBurnStatus(requestId: string): Promise<BurnStatus>;

  submitMintAuthorization(
    authorization: SignedMintAuthorization
  ): Promise<AuthorizationDeliveryResult>;

  submitReserveStatus(
    status: ReserveStatus
  ): Promise<ReserveStatusDeliveryResult>;

  submitRedemptionStatus(
    status: RedemptionStatus
  ): Promise<RedemptionStatusDeliveryResult>;

  healthCheck(): Promise<IntegrationHealth>;
}
```

If PayChain already exposes equivalent APIs, use them.

If not, add only the minimum required endpoints to PayChain.

