# 12. First Practical Release

The first release should focus on:

## PayKH

* Register tenant recipient profile
* Create payment order
* Detect bank payment
* Match payment
* Send signed confirmation to PayKH
* Prevent duplicate payment use
* Reconcile PayKH orders against bank transactions

## PayChain

* Receive reserve deposit
* Calculate reserve availability
* Send reserve status
* Approve mint request manually
* Issue signed mint authorization
* Confirm completed mint
* Reconcile reserve against supply

## Trustee Portal

* View bank transactions
* View unmatched payments
* View PayKH payment orders
* View PayChain reserve position
* Approve mint requests
* View reconciliation exceptions
* View audit history

---

# 13. Non-Negotiable Integration Rule

Never directly read or write the PayChain or PayKH production databases from the Trustee Platform.

Never allow PayChain or PayKH to directly read or write the Trustee database.

All financial coordination must occur through:

* Authenticated APIs
* Signed events
* Reconciliation files
* Approved operator workflows
* Immutable audit records
